# Build artifacts
/hayami
/hayami-tui
/dist/
*.exe

# Any other binary built in a worktree. A 35 MB test build was committed by a
# `git add -A` because the ignore list named only the two release binaries;
# these are the same programs under whatever name someone gave them.
#
# No negation for hayami-tui: `!` would *un-ignore* it and put a 21 MB binary
# back in reach of the next `git add -A`, which is the fault this line exists
# to close. The pattern covers it and that is the point.
/hayami-*

# Coverage
coverage.out
count.out

# makepkg's working directories and its output, when the package is built
# from this checkout.
packaging/arch/pkg/
packaging/arch/src/
packaging/arch/*.pkg.tar.zst

# The linter's per-checkout cache (Makefile lint target)
/.cache/
